    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0252" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.01/265: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-14T21:00:00+01:00">March 14, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2082. Dulanty, High Commissioner of Eire, asked Bruce<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d164-f1"/> if the Australian Government would intervene in opposing
                    the United States and British request to Eire to remove Axis representatives. I
                    understand this followed the Canadians’ refusal to intervene. Bruce with the
                    permission of his Government conveyed to me the following verbal statement
                    today: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Australian Government did not see its way to intervene so as to
                            secure the withdrawal of the American note and the attitude of the
                            Australian Government was that they were in accord with the American
                            request that the German and Japanese representatives be expelled and
                            hoped that the Eire Government would agree to take the action asked for
                            in the American note.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d164-f1" n="32" xml:id="d164-f1-content">
                <p>S. M. Bruce, Australian High Commissioner in London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
